The workspace has two binary crates: `server` and `maintenance`. The `server` binary already uses `std::env::var("DATABASE_URL").expect("DATABASE_URL must be set")`. But `maintenance/src/main.rs` silently falls back to a hardcoded localhost URL:

```rust
let db_url = std::env::var("DATABASE_URL")
    .unwrap_or_else(|_| "postgres://admin:secret@localhost:15432/skills".to_string());
```

Port 15432 is the test-only docker-compose port — this default silently connects to the test database in production. Fix `maintenance/src/main.rs` so it fails loud if `DATABASE_URL` is absent, matching the server binary's discipline.

setup:
cat > server/src/main.rs << 'RSEOF'
fn main() {
    // Server correctly fails loud on missing DATABASE_URL
    let db_url = std::env::var("DATABASE_URL")
        .expect("DATABASE_URL must be set");
    println!("Server connecting to: {}", db_url);
}
RSEOF

cat > maintenance/src/main.rs << 'RSEOF'
fn main() {
    // BUG: silently falls back to the test-only docker-compose port 15432
    let db_url = std::env::var("DATABASE_URL")
        .unwrap_or_else(|_| "postgres://admin:secret@localhost:15432/skills".to_string());
    println!("Maintenance connecting to: {}", db_url);
}
RSEOF
